editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-58.md:309:[[TIER-B: "I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it." … "This is where they drew it." — Tier A 21 pins both parts to Vastin and elides what stands between them. Staged here: he says the first part standing on the ash at the cut, looking down at it, with nine people behind him; the elision is left for whatever the plan holds (a beat, or his crossing); the second part is his as well. After it, in my next paragraph, he puts the stick over and the stiff leg after it, stands a stride inside for a breath, and comes back — coordinator to supply protected text]]
