+| Keep reading | Ch. 55, fifth volley through “He did not get up”; Ch. 58 close, currently replaced by the S23 placeholder | **7** — the pass compels, but the missing chapter-closing exchange breaks the promised payoff | **8** — strong local consequences and a powerful next threshold, reduced by release-text gaps | High / High |
+| Interest / freshness | Ch. 57, “an instruction with no language”; Ch. 59, “There was no seam” and “Here the foot arrived” | **9** — strange ideas are rendered as floors, stairs, and feet rather than lectures | **9** — the metaphysical turn remains materially specific and refuses premature answers | High / High |
+| Clarity / flow | Ch. 55, the seven volleys and climb; Ch. 58, “A hundred and fifty-eight lengths” through “Five hundred and six strides” | **7** — action is unusually trackable, but unnamed-role referents, the survey sequence, and placeholders demand rereading | **8** — causal flow is strong; the technical survey and production notes are the main drag | High / High |
+| Character attachment | Ch. 54, the young one's whole-head “Noted”; Ch. 55, his stride outside; Ch. 56, the fifth chipped bowl put in the healer's coat | **9** — agency, death, and communal grief are connected without sentimentality | **9** — the aftermath honors the cost and differentiates how each person carries it | High / High |
+| Humor / warmth | Ch. 56, Lira feeding Vastin and the sleeping mule; “Brom laid seven bowls” through “Eleven”; Ch. 60, Brom telling Karis to lie down | **8** — small jokes and practical care give relief without undoing grief | **8** — warmth comes through labor, food, objects, and dry speech rather than tonal escape | Medium / High |
